   "note": "Electorate c. 170,000-200,000 (high tax qualification). Guizot Law (1833) required a primary school in every commune => public schools. September Laws (1835) restricted the press. Loi Soult (1832): conscription by lot with substitution => mass conscription (limited). Slavery legal in the colonies until 27 April 1848 => labor slavery (game semantics: legal anywhere in the state). Catholicism 'religion of the majority' under the 1830 Charter; mapped as state religion."
